.TH TUI_READLINE 3 2026-10-03 "libtuikit 0.1" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_readline, tui_readline_opts_init \- read a line with editing, on a
terminal that is not full-screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/lineedit.h>
.PP
.B typedef struct tui_readline_opts {
.B "    int                    in_fd, out_fd;"
.B "    tui_history           *history;"
.B "    volatile sig_atomic_t *interrupt;"
.B "    int                    timeout_sec;"
.B "    unsigned               flags;"
.B } tui_readline_opts;
.PP
.BI "void tui_readline_opts_init(tui_readline_opts *" o );
.BI "int  tui_readline(const char *" prompt ", char *" buf ", size_t " size ,
.BI "                  const tui_readline_opts *" o );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tui_readline ()
is tg-cli's
.BR rl_readline ()
and mamind's
.BR line_editor_read ()
in one: it writes
.IR prompt ,
enters raw mode, lets the user edit one line on the current terminal line
with every key of
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3)
(history included), and on Enter writes a newline, restores the terminal
mode and returns the line.
A line longer than the terminal scrolls horizontally.
.PP
.BR tui_readline_opts_init ()
sets the defaults: standard input and output, no history, no interrupt
flag, no timeout.
.TP
.I history
browsed with Up and Down; an accepted, non-empty line is added to it.
.TP
.I interrupt
a flag the program's own signal handler sets: checked at least every 100
ms and whenever a signal interrupts the wait.
With
.B TUI_TERM_KEEP_ISIG
in
.I flags
Ctrl-C stays a signal key, as mamind needs; without it Ctrl-C is a key
that cancels.
.TP
.I timeout_sec
idle timeout: the call ends after this many seconds without a key (0:
none).
.PP
When the input is not a terminal \(em a pipe, a file, a test \(em the
prompt is written and a plain line is read with
.BR read (2),
CR dropped, as tg-cli does.
Esc is ignored while editing, as in tg-cli.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The length of the line in
.I buf
(NUL-terminated, truncated to
.IR size "\-1"
bytes), or:
.TP
.B TUI_READLINE_EOF
end of input, Ctrl-D on an empty line, the terminal hung up, or an error;
.TP
.B TUI_READLINE_CANCEL
Ctrl-C (signal keys off);
.TP
.B TUI_READLINE_INTERRUPT
.I *interrupt
became non-zero;
.TP
.B TUI_READLINE_TIMEOUT
no key for
.I timeout_sec
seconds.
.PP
All of them are negative; on any of them
.I buf
is the empty string.
The terminal mode is restored on every return.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3),
.BR tui_tty_raw_enter (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
